.TH EVCTL 1 "" "Peios" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
evctl \- query the Peios event, log and metric store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B evctl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I \(aqQUERY\(aq
.br
.B evctl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B \-\-file
.I PATH
.br
.B evctl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.B \-
.br
.B evctl help
.br
.B evctl version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B evctl
is the command-line client for
.BR eventd (8).
It sends one query in the PSPU observability query language to eventd's
query socket and writes the result to standard output.
.PP
The query is a single argument whose first word is
.BR EVENTS ,
.B LOGS
or
.BR METRIC ,
in any ASCII case. Quote the complete query so the shell cannot expand
patterns or split string literals:
.PP
.nf
.RS
evctl \(aqEVENTS kacs.* SINCE 1h ago TAKE 50\(aq
evctl \(aqLOGS FROM authd ERROR ONLY STREAM\(aq
evctl \(aqMETRIC cpu.usage SINCE 10m ago AVG\(aq
.RE
.fi
.PP
Exact standalone words such as
.B help
and
.B version
are commands rather than queries. The query can also be read from a file with
.BR \-\-file ,
or from standard input when the argument is
.BR \- .
.PP
eventd identifies the caller from the socket peer token and performs every
access check; records and fields the caller may not see are omitted.
.B evctl
never opens an eventd database itself.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fIFORMAT\fR"
Output encoding:
.B pretty
(the default, one self-describing record per line),
.B jsonl
(one JSON object per record; values JSON cannot carry are tagged objects),
or
.B msgpack
(a lossless sequence of MessagePack records, each preceded by its four-byte
little-endian payload length).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-socket " \fIPATH\fR"
Query socket to connect to. The default is
.IR /run/eventd/query.sock .
.TP
.BI \-\-file " PATH"
Read the query from the UTF-8 file
.IR PATH .
It cannot be combined with a query argument.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
Records are written to standard output; diagnostics and query errors to
standard error. Records in one result need not share a schema.
.PP
A result is published only once eventd confirms it complete (or, for a
streaming query, once its initial result is complete). Until then records are
held in an anonymous temporary spool, so an error part-way through never
leaves a partial result on standard output. After a streaming query's initial
result, new records are written as they arrive until
.B evctl
is interrupted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The query completed, or standard output was closed by its reader.
.TP
.B 1
The query could not be read, eventd could not be reached, the protocol
failed, eventd reported a query error, or output could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/eventd/query.sock
Default query socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR eventd (8)
.PP
The eventd manual and PSPU \(sc3 (the observability interfaces) at
https://learn.peios.org.
